    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0434" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/121: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Costa Rica (Eberhardt)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-11-11T18:00:00-05:00">November 11,
                            1932—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. Your despatch No. 1168, October 28.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d346-f1"/>
                    Associated Press despatch published in <hi rendition="#italic">La Prensa</hi>,
                    New York, dated San José, November 9, states that President Jiménez has announced that he will denounce the
                    Treaty of Peace and Amity of 1923.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d346-f2"/> Please report
                    by telegraph. Department does not desire you to discuss this matter with Costa
                    Rican officials beyond a possible inquiry for confirmation of this report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
